WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.170
Oh, I'm not lurking.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.260
Lester wanted to inspect the peep holes
because evidently some of them had been

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.500
installed backwards. So I said, well, I'll do
it. And he said, you know, the good time is 2

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.420
a.m., so I'm lying. I just wanted to say I'm
sorry.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.670
Oh. Apology accepted. Friendship mended.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.520
You're hired. No, no, I don't want to do this
show. I just want to hang out.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.860
Of course we'll do that all the time. Eight
shows a week and Broderick, you're fired.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:25.790
Wait a minute. Wait.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.490
This guy. I've seen him get out. Acted by a
horse.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.710
Maybe he was, but I'm guessing that horse
enjoyed himself on set that day because he

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:39.500
got to spend it with Charles Hayden Savidge,
who was probably kind to him and fed him a

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:47.300
fistful of oats out of his palm. And I bet
that horse didn't realize how good he had it

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:53.150
until he had another scene partner on another
set who just wrote them and wrote them and

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:57.830
wrote them and wrote them and wrote them and
wrote them and wrote them until he couldn't

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.450
take it anymore.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:05.030
And I bet that horse wishes he could say
sorry, but he can't. Not because he's a

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:09.710
horse, because he's a little messed up
emotionally, so all he can do is hate himself

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:14.600
and and wish he were dead for hurting his
best friend and that someone would turn him

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.440
into glue.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.240
Apology accepted.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.150
Okay, okay, I'll do the play.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.880
By the way, that horse won a patsy for that
scene.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.020
What's a patsy?

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.060
It's an Emmy for horses.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.390
You're still here? It's over.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.740
Go home.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:42.390
Go, you know, if you have any adjustments.
I'm very flexible and I've always found it's

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.170
best to be honest.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:52.200
I bet you would have made a much better.
Faris. Do you mean that? Oh, I want to, but

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.250
he's perfect.

